# Target C — C73 degree-four rhombic bulk frontier

**LEVEL I STATUS: STILL OPEN.**

Full proof: [target_c_degree_four_rhombic_bulk_2026-08-31.md](../../reports/target_c_degree_four_rhombic_bulk_2026-08-31.md).

C42/C49 show that all but `O(D)` bounded contact faces are strict unit rhombi. C73 upgrades that face statement to a vertex statement.

Let `m` be the force-visible contact-core population, `q=|B|` the loaded boundary
count, `h` the outer contact-face walk length, and

`Q=sum_bounded(k_f-4)`.

Euler and face counting give

`sum_v(4-deg_C v)=h+Q+4`,

while C49 gives

`h+Q<=4q-4`.

Every bounded quadrilateral face is a strict unit rhombus, so every one of its angles
lies in `(pi/3,2pi/3)`. An unloaded interior degree-three vertex therefore cannot be
surrounded only by quadrilateral faces: its three face angles would each be `<2pi/3`
but must sum to `2pi`.

The total boundary length of bounded nonquadrilateral faces is at most `5Q`. Hence

`N3<=h+5Q`.

Loaded vertices have degree at most three and unloaded vertices have degree `3,4,5`.
The curvature identity then gives

`N5<=4Q+3q-4`.

Therefore all but at most

`h+9Q+3q-4 <=39q-40 <39pi D`

contact-core vertices are interior degree-four vertices incident to four bounded strict
unit-rhombus faces.

## Interaction with C72

C72 radial cut transport says the near-zero single-port phase sends `Omega(D)` stress
through every graph layer and places almost all alpha mass on graph-outward, nearly
maximal-radial-progress contacts. C73 independently says there are only `O(D)` local
vertices where the carrier can use outer-boundary interaction, a nonquadrilateral
face, or unloaded degree three/five.

Thus a quadratic-size carrier is overwhelmingly a clean degree-four rhombic medium,
even if geometrically essential transverse edges have tiny alpha weight.

## Next target

Classify positive equilibrium through a clean degree-four strict-rhombus neighborhood
and propagate it through a connected clean region. The desired outcome is a rhombic
transport theorem: high stress either pays C68 transverse energy or follows a
fixed-direction strip until one of the `O(D)` C73 exceptional sites.

C73 does not assume or assert equality of opposite-edge stresses.